    "durationMs": 271833,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and verified end-to-end against every requirement.\n\n**Implementation** (`src/main.rs`): axum 0.8.4 router with sqlx as the persistence layer, connecting via `DATABASE_URL` (no hard-coded credentials). An embedded migration (`migrations/0001_create_links.sql`) creates the `links` table (`id BIGSERIAL` for creation order, unique `code`, `url`, `clicks`) and is applied at startup before serving — so `sh start.sh` (which execs the prebuilt release binary) applies pending migrations and serves on `0.0.0.0:8000` in the foreground. `README.md` documents how to start it.\n\n**Verified behavior:**\n- `POST /links` → 201 with `{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}`, submitted URL returned unchanged; auto-generated 8-char alphanumeric codes when `code` omitted (with retry on collision)\n- Duplicate custom code → 409 with `error`; invalid code (`ab`), non-http(s) URLs (`ftp://`, bare words), missing `url`, and malformed JSON all → 422 with `error`\n- `GET /links/{code}` → 200, unknown → 404 with `error`\n- `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with correct `Location`, clicks incremented exactly once per request (atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING`), unknown → 404\n- `GET /links` → `{\"items\": [...], \"total\": n}` in ascending creation order\n- Restarted the server via `start.sh`: data and click counts survived, migrations re-ran idempotently, uniqueness still enforced"
  }
